WHAT WAS MODIFIED
-----------------
Twelve patches. Patches 0001-0002 are against upstream 0.20.4; patches
0003-0012 are a series against a stated commit of this fork (see BASELINE.md).
All of them concern several Hermes sessions sharing ONE self-hosted model
backend.

  patches/0001-status-bar-own-vs-backend-accounting.patch
      cli.py -- the status bar's delegation segment now distinguishes this
      session's own live subagents from the shared backend's global occupancy,
      and reports how many dispatch slots are actually free.

  patches/0002-delegation-explicit-child-context-window.patch
      tools/delegate_tool.py -- a subagent's context window is resolved and
      logged explicitly at dispatch time instead of being inherited implicitly
      from the parent profile's model.context_length. Adds an "auto" ladder
      sized from live backend pressure, plus a runtime child-concurrency cap.

  patches/0003-pool-broker-share-bounded-grant-ceilings.patch
      agent/pool_policy.py, agent/pool_broker.py, agent/context_compressor.py
      -- the cross-session KV-pool broker bounds the ceilings it GRANTS rather
      than only the reservations it can measure. Adds
      derive_window_ceilings(), a grant invariant over the worst case, and
      grandfathering for a session already above its share.

  patches/0004-portability-explicit-encodings-pool-overflow.patch
      agent/pool_broker.py, agent/overflow_router.py,
      tools/goal_resume_supervisor.py -- explicit encodings, and two
      POSIX-only calls annotated rather than disguised.

  patches/0005-auxiliary-work-yields-to-interactive-lanes.patch
      agent/auxiliary_client.py, agent/title_generator.py,
      agent/background_review.py, cli.py -- background auxiliary work carries
      an explicit low request priority, a one-shot run is no longer classified
      interactive, and a one-shot session skips the title model call.

  patches/0006-overflow-tree-view-markers-and-route-hotkey.patch
      tools/delegate_tool.py, cli.py -- a subagent routed to the hosted
      overflow provider is marked in the tree view with a route line at spawn
      and an outcome line at finish, and a hotkey toggles the route.

  patches/0007-goal-loop-interrupt-provenance-and-blocked-verdict.patch
      hermes_cli/goals.py, hermes_cli/cli_commands_mixin.py, cli.py,
      tools/goal_resume_supervisor.py -- interrupts carry provenance, so a
      machine interrupt is no longer labelled as the human's Ctrl+C; `blocked`
      becomes a first-class judge verdict; `/goal resume` re-arms the
      continuation; the resume supervisor gains the stalled-active class.

  patches/0008-status-bar-live-shared-pool-share.patch
      hermes_cli/pool_share.py (new), cli.py -- the status bar's ctx
      denominator becomes the live share the broker granted, not the static
      profile window. Display only, and the tests enforce that.

  patches/0009-goal-loop-bounded-machine-interrupt-rearm.patch
      hermes_cli/goals.py, cli.py -- the machine-interrupt re-arm 0007 added
      is bounded, so a permanently wedged route pauses with an auto-resumable
      reason instead of spinning.

  patches/0010-pool-share-read-the-kv-pool-not-the-context-length.patch
      hermes_cli/pool_share.py -- read the KV pool as the share bound, not the
      per-request context length. A field-selection bug that was invisible
      while the two values coincided.

  patches/0011-goal-loop-delegate-the-wait-to-a-watcher.patch
      hermes_cli/goal_watchers.py (new), hermes_cli/goals.py,
      tools/goal_resume_supervisor.py, gateway/slash_commands.py -- a goal
      delegates its wait to a zero-model-call watcher instead of parking
      itself, with a barrier age ceiling and a quote-verified probe for other
      advanceable work.

  patches/0012-pool-broker-prefill-capacity-child-throttle.patch
      agent/pool_broker.py -- the child-dispatch throttle is re-keyed off free
      device VRAM onto slots, prefill backlog and pool residency, after a KV
      offload took free VRAM out of the capacity path.

upstream-modified/tools/delegate_tool.py is pristine upstream 0.20.4 with
patch 0002 applied, provided so the change is readable in full.

WHAT WAS CHANGED FOR PUBLICATION
--------------------------------
Patch 0002 as it runs on its original deployment carried three
deployment-specific strings. They are replaced here; nothing else differs:

  * the default backend probe URL is a private address on the original
    deployment. Published as http://127.0.0.1:30000 (SGLang's own default
    bind). Override with HERMES_KV_BACKEND. The probe fails open, so a wrong
    value costs the sizing signal and nothing else.
  * a profile name in one comment is generalised to "the parent (main-thread)
    profile".
  * the served model is referred to generically rather than by its local lane
    name. The architectural reasoning is unchanged and applies to any
    hybrid-attention model that pins a fixed recurrent state per in-flight
    request.

Patches 0003-0012 were scrubbed the same way, mechanically. 82 lines were
substituted in total, each one line for one line, and each patch that carries
any of them says so in its own header.

The scrub is confined to the lines a patch ADDS, with one deliberate exception.
A context or removed line is quoted from the base the patch applies to, so
rewriting one stops the patch applying -- EXCEPT where that base is an earlier
patch in this same series, in which case the quoted line is our own published
output and MUST be rewritten to match it. Exactly one line is of that kind: a
docstring line in patch 0011 whose pre-image is a line patch 0007 adds. See
"What could not be scrubbed" below for the lines that are not.

The classes:

  * PRIVATE ADDRESS. A private backend address becomes 127.0.0.1, with the
    engine port published as 30000 and the second lane as 30001, following the
    placeholder convention already used by patch 0002 and ops/README.md.
    5 occurrences, all in test fixtures.
  * ABSOLUTE PATHS. An absolute fleet log path becomes "<stack>/..."
    (ops/README.md's placeholder for the serving host's stack root), and an
    absolute agent-home path becomes the tilde form "~/.hermes/...", which is
    what patch 0002 already publishes. One of the two is a test that reads the
    live profile on purpose, so it is republished as
    Path("~/.hermes/.../config.yaml").expanduser() -- same behaviour, and it
    still pytest.skips when the file is absent.
  * LIVE PROCESS IDS. Four (two in a comment, two in a test's expected
    `grandfathered` list) become 900001-900004. Ordering is preserved, which is
    all the assertion depends on.
  * SESSION IDS. Three become synthetic ids of the same shape.
  * AN INTERNAL PANE REFERENCE. Generalised to "the peer pane".
  * THE SERVING HOST'S LOCAL NICKNAME, in three comments, becomes "the serving
    host" -- ops/README.md's own placeholder for it.
  * THE JUDGE-VERDICT FIXTURE CORPUS, which is the one case where a mechanical
    scrub would have destroyed the artifact. Patch 0007's regression corpus is
    five production judge verdicts and patch 0011's is a verbatim park, and
    those exact strings are the evidence a classifier and a quote-verification
    filter have to handle -- paraphrase them and the test no longer tests
    anything. Three of the five, and the park, named a third-party platform
    and described a blocked commercial submission. They are therefore
    SUBSTITUTED, not paraphrased: structurally equivalent synthetic strings
    with the same shape, the same trigger words ("blocked pending", "still
    pending", "upload-ready", "login from the owner"), the same quoted spans,
    an invented platform name and invented subject matter. The two verdicts
    that carried no third-party subject are verbatim. No classifier pattern
    was touched, and the proof that the substitution preserved what mattered
    is that those suites still pass -- see BASELINE.md.

WHAT COULD NOT BE SCRUBBED, AND IS DISCLOSED INSTEAD
----------------------------------------------------
A patch's REMOVED and CONTEXT lines are quoted from the base it applies to.
Rewrite one and the patch stops applying to its stated base, which is the
property BASELINE.md exists to prove. So the scrub above is confined to added
lines, and everything the other lines carry was audited rather than edited.
What they carry, exhaustively:

  * one change held back entirely. A correction to an overflow status message
    (fork commit 3272a15, agent/overflow_router.py, +10 -2) REMOVES a line
    that is itself an absolute home path. It is therefore documented-only:
    described in README.md, not shipped as a patch. Nothing else in the series
    was held back.
  * this deployment's internal tracker ids (bd-dre-*) appear in comments and
    docstrings throughout, including on eight removed lines. They are opaque
    references with no content behind them in this repository, and a
    half-scrubbed set would be worse than an honest one, so they are retained.
  * a profile name ("architect") appears in comments and as a test fixture
    value. Patch 0002 generalised it because there it sat on a single added
    comment line and was free to change; here it is woven through context and
    removed lines and fixture values.
  * the hosted overflow provider is named. It is a public inference vendor and
    "cerebras" is a config provider key and a Decision field value; renaming
    it would make the diff fiction. No key, endpoint, account identifier or
    key path is published.
  * the serving host's local nickname survives twice, both on context lines
    this series does not author: one pre-existing test function name
    (test_no_ssh_to_delta_under_pytest, in patch 0012) and one comment above a
    constant patch 0012 edits. Its three occurrences on ADDED lines were
    substituted; see above. No session ids survive -- all three were
    substitutable.
  * commit hashes of this fork appear in comments, and are also how BASELINE.md
    states each patch's base. They are deliberate; they resolve only in the
    private tree.
  * files this series adds carry the fork's house header, "Copyright (c) 2026
    Ligandal, Inc. All rights reserved." The NOTICE above governs: everything
    in this directory, these modifications included, is offered under the same
    MIT terms as the upstream work. That header is the fork's boilerplate, not
    a reservation of rights against this publication.

Not present anywhere in these patches: credentials, API keys or tokens; any
routable address or public host name (the only addresses that appear are
loopback placeholders); model weights or checkpoints; traffic-derived
artifacts; customer, partner or third-party-platform names other than the
inference vendor named above. The only email address in them is the author
line each patch carries, which is the same address every commit in this
repository carries.

A quantity of surrounding operational tooling on the original deployment is
deliberately NOT published, because it encodes that deployment's architecture
rather than anything reusable. The reusable part of it -- the patterns -- is
written up generically in docs/design-notes.md.
